# Event Driven Guidelines

## Event naming
Past tense only. Examples: `UserCreated`, `MessageSent`, `MessageRead`.

## Rules
- Events represent facts that already happened
- Events are immutable
- Consumers/handlers must be idempotent when processing side effects

## Structure (domain events)
- EventId / type, OccurredAt, aggregate id, payload, version where applicable
- Publish via shared event bus; handle in `infrastructure/handlers/*`

## Patterns in this codebase
- Domain event → `ChatRealtimeBroadcastHandler`, analytics, notifications
- Prefer outbox-style reliability for critical cross-system delivery (when introducing new integrations)

## Anti-patterns
- Using events as commands
- Mutating event payloads in handlers
- Synchronous cross-module coupling instead of events or explicit ports
